 | `avm1_tabindex_read_first_coerce` | A READ of `this.tabIndex` before the first set materialises the root's native accessor, so the later sets COERCE (`undefined`, then `-2147483648 -2147483648 5 -2147483648`). Golden = **FP32** (`t11_read_first.txt`); SWF = `make_fixtures.py` `t11` |
 | `avm1_tabindex_mtasc_class_main` | MTASC class bootstrap: the DoInitAction's unresolved `GetVariable "Test"` (a scope lookup that misses the root's own properties) materialises the accessor, so `main`'s `_root.tabIndex = "s"` COERCES; also `m.tabIndex = 0; m.tabIndex = "t"` → INT_MIN on a fresh child. Golden = **FP32** (`w1-disposition-audit/L3b_tabindex_v8/flash.txt`); source `Test.as` (MTASC `-version 8`) |
 | `avm1_tabindex_child_null` | Numeric-string and `null` coercion on clips (s29 `w3-interim3-residuals`): timeline sprite `c.tabIndex = "x"` → `-2147483648`; script-created `m.tabIndex = "5"` → `5`; `m.tabIndex = null` → **`undefined`** (null unsets like undefined; we used to print `0`). Golden = **FP32** (`w1-local-oracles/w2b-tabindex.t_child_numstr_null.txt`); SWF = `w2b-tabindex-oracle/make_fixture.py`. Owner: `action.c` `actionSetMember` tabIndex block |
+| `avm2_stroke_curve_scale_s1s4` | **AS3 drawing-API curve flattening at HIGH is 0.01 px** (s30 `w2-stroke-geometry-land`; `avm2_display.c` `gfx_curve_tol_scale` → `gfx_flatten_cmds`). The acid-shapes squiggles (`curveTo` pairs, `lineStyle(4 / 16, 0x49D0D7)`, round caps) at scale ×1 and ×4, translation 0 and .3 px, 16 cells. Golden = **FP32 HIGH** (`fp32.lnx.high.png`, byte-equal to the Windows capture). **The budgets are OUR measured outliers after the change, NOT a Flash-parity verdict**: Flash's curved stroke is wider than the exact offset by a half-width-dependent excess we do not model (about +0.2 px per side at hw 2, +0.7 at hw 8, a +1.2 px plateau at hw ≥ 32), so the rows can never reach 0. They guard the 0.01 px rule: lyon's 0.1 px (`SWF_AVM2_CURVE_FINE=0`) exceeds every check. `Test.as` is the mxmlc source |
+| `avm2_stroke_curve_scale_s16_w4_k0` | Same guard, one 2-curve squiggle at ×16, `lineStyle(4)` (hw 32 px). FP32 golden, budgets = our outliers after the change (see `avm2_stroke_curve_scale_s1s4`). The flatten tolerance is in LOCAL pixels, so at ×16 the residual chord deficit is 16× larger: a scale-aware rebuild is the open lead |
+| `avm2_stroke_curve_scale_s16_w4_k1` | Same guard, the single-curve V squiggle at ×16, `lineStyle(4)` |
+| `avm2_stroke_curve_scale_s16_w16_k0` | Same guard, the 2-curve squiggle at ×16, `lineStyle(16)` (hw 128 px) |
+| `avm2_stroke_curve_scale_s16_w16_k1` | Same guard, the V squiggle at ×16, `lineStyle(16)` |
+| `avm2_stroke_translucent_round` | Translucent wide closed round strokes at HIGH (`lineStyle(10, 0xFF0000, .5)` drawRect + drawCircle, `lineStyle(10, 0x0000FF, .5)` drawRoundRect, `lineStyle(20, 0x00AA00, .5)` drawEllipse). FP32 golden; budgets = our outliers after the change. It also prices the AVM2 seam twin at HIGH: a `gfx_build_stroke` width gate that joins instead of capping the seam leaves the render md5-identical, so there is no visible seam double-blend at HIGH and no gate was landed |
